//ERR 18 10 18 11
//MSG="No candidate found for this function call"

// 66e_using_the_value_of_a_void_function.cpl rejects a void value used in
// arithmetic. This one rejects it after a trip through a variable: binding a
// void result is allowed (13_known_bugs/25_binding_a_void_result_to_a_variable.cpl),
// but the variable is still not a value, so there is no `print` overload that
// takes it.
//
// The regression this guards: erasing void variables in codegen must not erase
// them from the type system. If the binding ever made `r` look like a value,
// this case would start compiling and emit a call to a print that does not exist.

fn nothing
    ret

fn main
    r = nothing()
    out "{r}"
